"Locations gain a SURFACE vs INSIDE distinction. Standing in a SURFACE location, you can see and be seen by entities sharing the location OF your location, recursively through surface relations - so outdoor rooms nest into a greater outdoor location (a field, a forest), outdoor locations sit on a world surface, and ONE sky entity is visible from everywhere outdoors. INSIDE locations (caves, buildings) cut the chain. Movement addition: a large enough entity may EXIT a surface location directly into the outer location - whether the destination reads as surface or interior follows the location type of the initial location. Implies: visibility derivation over the location tree (client rendering + targeting reach), a location-type field on rooms/maps (authored via themes), size-gated exit as an offered action on the location itself, and the sky as a world-level entity. Not started - recorded direction (2026-08-15)."